     Project Overview
This project performs end-to-end analysis of an insurance claims dataset containing 1,000 records across 39 original columns. The goal is to uncover actionable insights around claim patterns, fraud detection, customer segmentation, and risk profiling — delivering cleaned data, pivot-based analytics, and a professional Excel dashboard ready for management presentation.
The analysis answers four core business questions:

What are the trends in claims by policy type, region, incident type, and time?
Which customer segments or locations have the highest claim rates?
What is the distribution of fraudulent vs. non-fraudulent claims, and what factors are common in fraud cases?
What is the relationship between policy details (premium, deductible) and claim amounts/frequency?


